---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Leadership — Conatus Real Estate Inc."
  description="Ted Farry — President of Conatus Real Estate, CEO of Homestead Affordable, COO of Fortune Acquisitions. Nearly 25 years of institutional single-family residential real estate experience."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container--narrow">
      <p class="page-label">Leadership</p>
      <h1>Built by <span class="accent">operators</span></h1>

      <div class="leader-profile">
        <div class="leader-info">
          <h2>Ted Farry</h2>
          <p class="leader-title">President & Founder, Conatus Real Estate Inc.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="prose">
          <p class="lead">
            Ted Farry has nearly 25 years of experience in single-family residential
            real estate, spanning institutional acquisitions, asset management,
            affordable housing, and technology platform development. He is the
            President &amp; Founder of Conatus Real Estate Inc., Founder &amp; CEO
            of Homestead Affordable, and COO of Fortune Acquisitions.
          </p>

          <h3>Operational Background</h3>
          <p>
            Ted's career is rooted in building SFR platforms from the ground up. As
            COO of Fortune Acquisitions, a multi-market institutional acquisitions
            platform, he built and led a team that executed over 3,500 purchase and
            sale transactions across multiple markets. Before Fortune, he built an
            1,100-property workforce housing portfolio and acquisitions platform from
            scratch in two years at True Lane Homes, the SFR arm of a Southern
            California-based single family office. Ted leveraged his extensive industry
            network in the building of each of these platforms.
          </p>
          <p>
            His asset management experience spans the full SFR lifecycle —
            acquisitions, disposition, compliance, and Housing Choice Voucher (HCV)
            operations including lease-ups, housing authority coordination, inspection
            management, and compliance operations. This isn't theoretical knowledge —
            it's the result of managing real portfolios with real tenants and real
            regulatory requirements.
          </p>

          <h3>Homestead Affordable</h3>
          <p>
            Ted founded Homestead Affordable to apply his institutional SFR expertise
            to workforce and affordable housing. Homestead acquires and operates
            single-family rental portfolios with a focus on communities underserved
            by institutional capital, leveraging the same operational infrastructure
            and industry network that powered his work building platforms at Fortune
            Acquisitions and True Lane Homes.
          </p>

          <h3>Technology &amp; AI</h3>
          <p>
            Through Conatus Real Estate, Ted builds AI-powered operations platforms
            for regulated industries. He recognized early that the operational
            bottlenecks in these industries aren't solved by off-the-shelf SaaS
            products — the problems are too specific, the compliance requirements
            too nuanced, and the workflows too interconnected for generic tools. The
            answer is purpose-built platforms — and now, AI makes it possible to
            build them faster and make them smarter.
          </p>
          <p>
            Every platform Conatus builds leverages Claude's intelligence through MCP
            integrations, autonomous agent workflows, and AI-driven analysis pipelines.
            Ted's development practice is AI-native: Claude isn't an add-on to the
            development process, it's core infrastructure for both building platforms
            and powering them in production.
          </p>

          <h3>Approach</h3>
          <p>
            Over the course of his career, Ted has developed a juxtaposed expertise
            in physical real estate operations and analytics-based quantitative
            problem solving. He has an ability to bring together all parts of an
            organization to solve problems from a holistic viewpoint — and his
            consulting approach starts with understanding the operational reality on
            the ground before writing a line of code. Technology should serve
            operations, not the other way around.
          </p>
          <p>
            Ted is recognized as an expert resource in the SFR community and is a
            frequent speaker on industry conference panels. He earned an M.B.A. from
            Pepperdine University and a B.A. in Mathematics and Philosophy from
            Linfield College. He holds a California Real Estate Broker license.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="leader-contact">
          <a href="mailto:houses@conatusre.com" class="btn btn--primary">Get in Touch</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .page-label {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    color: var(--color-accent);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
  }

  h1 {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-xl);
  }

  .leader-profile {
    margin-top: var(--space-lg);
  }

  .leader-info {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-xl);
    padding-bottom: var(--space-lg);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .leader-info h2 {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-xs);
  }

  .leader-title {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    color: var(--color-accent);
    font-weight: 500;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .lead {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-xl);
  }

  .leader-contact {
    margin-top: var(--space-xl);
    padding-top: var(--space-xl);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }
</style>
